# milestone_0030 remote-build workload of the V4 Linux service (DESIGN s5, 13.2, 14.2, r4.1, r4.1b).
# SOURCE_AUTHORED / NOT_RUN. Lib layer: never imports the service module (C) or any `app.` module (F5).
#
# This file holds the pre-transfer settle (r4.1b), the open authority (14.4) and the executor `HostRemoteBuildExecutorV3`
# with its port (F5). The service module (C) holds the executor and drives it; a pre-transfer failure settles here.
#
# r4.1b: before the admission transfer nothing has run (no container, no source opened), but the execute already
# begun the row and committed the charge. A pre-transfer failure (an open-side `request_bytes` mismatch, a refused
# open authority, an expired deadline before start) therefore settles the executing row `cancelled` / `no-workload`
# through the 14.2 settle arm, which releases the charge on the single journal writer. `agent_consumed` is set only at
# the transfer, so the incarnation stays usable; the caller then drops the build holder and the slot clears through
# the existing ended path of the slot check.
